        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "cb714ed8-fc44-5e33-9769-90ab463202c2",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Division of Mayo, Adelaide, South Australia, Adelaide Hills, Fleurieu Peninsula, Kangaroo Island, Crafers, Stirling\n- People: Rebekha Sharkie, Jamie Briggs\n- Organizations: Nick Xenophon Team, Australian House of Representatives\n- Events: 2016 federal election\n\nFacts:\n- The Division of Mayo is an Australian electoral division located to the east, south, south-east, and south-west of Adelaide in South Australia.\n- The Division of Mayo includes the Adelaide Hills, Fleurieu Peninsula, and Kangaroo Island.\n- The Division of Mayo includes the towns of Bridgewater, Crafers, Echunga, Gumeracha, Hahndorf, Kingscote, Langhorne Creek, Lobethal, Macclesfield, Mount Barker, Myponga, Oakbank, Stirling, Strathalbyn, Victor Harbor, Woodside, Yankalilla, and part of Birdwood.\n- In 2016, Rebekha Sharkie began representing the Division of Mayo after defeating Liberal candidate Jamie Briggs at the 2016 federal election.\n- Rebekha Sharkie was the first Nick Xenophon Team member elected to the Australian House of Representatives.\n- Crafers is a town in the Adelaide Hills to the south-east of Adelaide, South Australia.\n- Crafers is technically considered an outer suburb of Adelaide.\n- Many residents of Crafers commute to Adelaide for work.\n- Locals consider Crafers to be more a suburb of the nearby township of Stirling.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "530e6823-0d17-5d84-a7f9-d5cb046f93a2",
        "text": "Page: Division of Mayo. Sentence: The Division of Mayo is an Australian electoral division located to the east, south, south-east and south-west of Adelaide, South Australia.\nPage: Division of Mayo. Sentence: It takes in the Adelaide Hills, Fleurieu Peninsula and Kangaroo Island, including the towns of Bridgewater, Crafers, Echunga, Gumeracha, Hahndorf, Kingscote, Langhorne Creek, Lobethal, Macclesfield, Mount Barker, Myponga, Oakbank, Stirling, Strathalbyn, Victor Harbor, Woodside, Yankalilla, and part of Birdwood.\nPage: Crafers, South Australia. Sentence: The town of Crafers is in the Adelaide Hills to the south-east of Adelaide, South Australia.\nPage: Crafers, South Australia. Sentence: Although technically considered to be an outer suburb of Adelaide, with many residents commuting to the city to work, locals consider Crafers to be more a suburb of the nearby township of Stirling.\nPage: Rebekha Sharkie. Sentence: Representing the Division of Mayo since defeating Liberal Jamie Briggs at the 2016 federal election, she is the first Nick Xenophon Team member to be elected to the Australian House of Representatives.",
